~ start
Clerk: The two claims are before you. Neither is yet your finding.
- Hear the claimant's statement
	Claimant: {{assignment_context.client_name}} states: {{assignment_context.client_statement}}
	=> particulars
- Hear the opposing party's statement
	Opposing party: {{assignment_context.opposing_name}} states: {{assignment_context.opposing_statement}}
	=> particulars
- Read the claimant's particulars
	Clerk: {{assignment_context.client_record}}
	=> particulars
- Read the opposing party's particulars
	Clerk: {{assignment_context.opposing_record}}
	=> particulars
- Ask what question the docket puts to you
	Clerk: {{assignment_context.requested_result}}
	=> END

~ particulars
Clerk: These are the claims and particulars supplied with the docket. They remain claims until you enter a disposition.
- Return to the docket => END
